# Line endings.
#
# The repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so the working tree
# is CRLF. That is harmless for TypeScript, but a shell script checked out with
# CRLF fails inside a Linux container with the notoriously unhelpful
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — the \r becomes part of the
# interpreter path. Anything executed by a Linux image is pinned to LF.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
